"""Local editorial revisions made after duplicate-decision QA.
These are preparation decisions, not newly asserted environmental facts.
"""
from .core import ROWS
EDITS={
'Orkla':'Choose the host and allocated stretch before arranging accommodation. Ask whether the booking includes a ghillie, instruction and a complete outfit or only access to the water. Keep any equipment purchase conditional on the host’s current presentation recommendation rather than using another Norwegian river’s list.',
'Namsen':'Compare a bank-based salmon day with any boat-supported option the host actually offers. Establish where you meet, who handles transport and how the fishing session is organized. Those practical answers should determine rod portability and clothing; the river’s reputation is not a substitute for a specific plan.',
'Lough Mask':'Begin with the guide’s launch point and the intended fishing style. Ask how much casting space each angler has, whether a supplied rod is available and which small selection of flies is useful. Keep an accessible dry layer in the boat instead of carrying a complete bank-fishing camp.',
'Lough Carra':'Fit the outing to the amount of time you can spend fishing after transfers. Request the exact meeting place and an explanation of the proposed lake method. An unfamiliar lake is a good reason to use a local boatman before buying extra line systems or a large fly assortment.',
'River Tay':'Specify whether the goal is learning salmon presentation or spending a full session on allocated water. Ask the host to describe the actual casting approach and any supplied equipment. Match the booking to the group’s ability rather than choosing a rod on the strength of the river name alone.',
'River Spey':'Discuss casting instruction explicitly when enquiring about a Spey trip. Confirm the chosen beat, room to cast and the outfit recommended by its host; do not assume a particular technique simply because the river shares its name. Pack the confirmed setup and a short replacement list.',
'River Dee':'Ask how the beat visit is organized: meeting time, fishing rotation, local assistance and any walking between positions. Separate those arrangements from accommodation. A host-confirmed clothing and tackle list is more useful than buying a complete Scottish salmon kit before the actual water is allocated.',
'Semois / Herbeumont':'Use Herbeumont to narrow the enquiry to a particular river reach, then ask which target and technique fit your intended visit. Compare a guided session with a bank-access outing as different arrangements. Carry only a small working tackle selection once those details have been confirmed.',
'Eau d’Heure Lakes':'Choose the specific lake and shore before treating this lake group as one fishing destination. Ask whether your plan is bank-based or uses a boat, and confirm any equipment available locally. Keep the target unresolved until the water manager or guide identifies the actual opportunity.',
'Chiese / Val di Fumo':'Establish the approach and return arrangement for the selected Val di Fumo outing. Ask how much walking is involved and whether a guided fishing day includes equipment. Keep the tackle compact enough to leave room for appropriate layers rather than borrowing the packing list from a roadside river.',
'Avisio / CK reach':'Use the reach identifier when asking the fishery about this trip; a general Avisio enquiry may refer to different water. Confirm the target, recommended presentation and assistance available for a first visit. Buy replacement flies or lures only after the local specification is known.',
'Adige / NKC reach':'Confirm the NKC reach and the actual access point before organizing the day. Ask the local fishery to distinguish its proposed method from those used elsewhere on the Adige. The resulting line and terminal-tackle requirements should be matched to existing equipment before adding purchases.',
'Lake Śniardwy':'Discuss the boat plan and a weather alternative when enquiring about Śniardwy. Clarify whether the guide expects a target-focused pike day or a more varied outing. Keep personal equipment limited to what is missing from the confirmed boat inventory, not every lure suitable for the Masurian region.',
'Lake Niegocin':'Treat Niegocin as a specific enquiry within the operator’s wider guiding area. Agree on the meeting point and fishing objective before choosing accommodation or transportation. Ask whether a beginner can use supplied equipment so a first lake outing does not require an unnecessary rod purchase.',
'Kanina River':'Ask the guide what a Kanina day would involve for your level of experience: walking, casting, instruction and time actually fishing. Let that itinerary determine a compact equipment list. A river mentioned in a regional programme still needs a confirmed target and stretch before it becomes your plan.',
'Iugovska River':'Request a named session on the Iugovska rather than assuming it is interchangeable with the operator’s other Bulgarian rivers. Confirm the meeting arrangement, fishing method and available tackle. Keep travel equipment adaptable until the guide has chosen the water for your dates.',
'Ruhudji River':'Build the Ruhudji visit around Samaki Camp’s own equipment guidance. Ask how rods and working tackle are stored in the fishing boat and which spare connections are useful. Keep the main tigerfish outfit accessible during transfers instead of packing it beneath unrelated safari luggage.',
'Bulago Island — Lake Victoria':'Ask whether fishing is arranged from the island or requires a separate mainland launch and transfer. Confirm the Nile perch method, skipper and tackle provision before adding equipment to your luggage. A general island stay should not be mistaken for a fully arranged fishing package.',
'Kalangala islands — Lake Victoria':'Choose the actual island base and ask the outfitter how the fishing day connects with your accommodation. Agree on return transport and which tackle the boat supplies. The Kalangala area reference identifies an enquiry lead, not one universal launch point or fixed daily itinerary.',
'Ocotal':'Establish whether the offer is nearshore or offshore and ask how much fishing time remains after the run. Your list should follow that method and boat arrangement, not the beach-resort label. Confirm supplied tackle before choosing a travel outfit.',
'Carrillo':'Separate fishing hours from travel time when comparing Carrillo offers. Ask about the intended grounds, crew-provided tackle and conditions that change the outing. Keep a small dry day bag ready, and do not buy an offshore setup without an explicit skipper recommendation.',
'Chub Cay — Berry Islands':'Establish a specific boat and target before comparing Chub Cay packages. Clarify whether lodging, dock transfer and fishing equipment are included or separate. A marina or island name does not by itself establish a charter, so confirm the crew and fishing plan before finalizing travel.',
'Cayo Largo':'For Cayo Largo, obtain a fresh written confirmation of the fishing programme and transport chain before selecting dates. The source warns of infrastructure disruption in Cuba. Keep this as a research lead rather than active inventory, and defer specialized purchases until the operator confirms the arrangements.',
'Cayo Romano':'Ask the operator whether the Cayo Romano programme is currently running and how guests reach its fishing base. The source’s Cuba disruption warning makes those confirmations more important than choosing tackle early. Confirm the actual flats method and guide-supplied equipment only after the operating plan is clear.',
'Zapata':'Start a Zapata enquiry with present operating status, transfers and contingency arrangements. The linked programme is reference coverage, not a live booking offer, and its source flags Cuba-wide disruptions. Request an exact itinerary before treating a destination name as a complete saltwater fishing plan.',
'Cayo Santa María':'Keep the Cayo Santa María listing separate from a promise of a functioning holiday package. Ask for current transport, accommodation and guided-fishing confirmation in light of the source’s disruption notice. Once those are established, choose the target-specific kit rather than buying a general Cuba flats bundle.',
'Laamu Atoll':'Keep the offshore charter distinct from a shallow-flat day. Ask about the boat’s range, heavy-tackle provision and weather alternatives before comparing packages. Confirm whether the operator arranges transfers from your particular island, since an atoll-wide label is not a meeting point.'
}
for r in ROWS:
 if r['place'] in EDITS:r['decision']=EDITS[r['place']]
